  "note": "the metric is materially wrong but not decisively so. Switching endpoint distance for object distance lifts MST-spanning-link reachability at 5 um from 64.9% to 75.7% on tier10 and from 47.7% to 56.8% on the full population, and makes 280 labelled atoms proposable that had no endpoint row at all -- but it does not approach EXP-060's 90% bar, so proximity's failure is not an artefact of measuring from tips. It also changes the ground truth: 463 of 3538 spanning links on the full population differ between the two metrics, so EXP-060B's panel was scored against a partly different answer key. Object distance should replace endpoint distance everywhere downstream on those grounds, not because it rescues the ball.",
